WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.234
New fundraising totals are

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:02.302
giving us insight

00:00:02.302 --> 00:00:03.103
into which Republican

00:00:03.103 --> 00:00:04.871
candidates are gaining steam

00:00:04.871 --> 00:00:06.406
and who is falling behind.

00:00:06.406 --> 00:00:07.007
Those numbers

00:00:07.007 --> 00:00:08.375
are even more important than usual

00:00:08.375 --> 00:00:09.776
since small donors

00:00:09.776 --> 00:00:10.777
will help decide

00:00:10.777 --> 00:00:11.611
whether Republican

00:00:11.611 --> 00:00:13.313
candidates can make the debate stage

00:00:13.313 --> 00:00:14.614
next month.

00:00:15.715 --> 00:00:17.183
And joining me now is a candidate

00:00:17.183 --> 00:00:18.952
who says he has already met

00:00:18.952 --> 00:00:20.787
those fundraising requirements, former

00:00:20.787 --> 00:00:22.856
New Jersey Governor Chris Christie.

00:00:22.889 --> 00:00:24.391
Governor Christie, thanks for joining us.

00:00:24.391 --> 00:00:25.859
Your campaign reports

00:00:25.859 --> 00:00:27.961
having raised $1.7 million

00:00:27.961 --> 00:00:29.262
in the first 25 days

00:00:29.262 --> 00:00:30.797
of your presidential bid.

00:00:30.797 --> 00:00:32.365
That's more than Mike Pence.

00:00:32.365 --> 00:00:32.932
But behind

00:00:32.932 --> 00:00:34.734
not only Donald Trump and Ron DeSantis,

00:00:34.734 --> 00:00:36.503
but also Nikki Haley and Tim Scott.

00:00:36.503 --> 00:00:39.239
They were in the race longer than you.

00:00:39.272 --> 00:00:39.939
We should note.

00:00:39.939 --> 00:00:41.574
But you are going to have to do a lot

00:00:41.574 --> 00:00:42.976
better than that in the next quarter.

00:00:42.976 --> 00:00:44.244
So how are you going to achieve that?

00:00:46.713 --> 00:00:48.014
Well, look, Jake, if

00:00:48.014 --> 00:00:49.949
we continue to raise money at the pace

00:00:49.949 --> 00:00:51.384
we've been raising it,

00:00:51.384 --> 00:00:52.585
we're going to do just fine.

00:00:52.585 --> 00:00:55.855
I mean, as you noted, Tim Scott transfer

00:00:55.855 --> 00:00:57.390
the significant amount of money

00:00:57.390 --> 00:00:59.059
from his Senate campaign.

00:00:59.059 --> 00:01:00.393
Nikki Haley, he's been in the race,

00:01:00.393 --> 00:01:02.462
I think, since February.

00:01:02.462 --> 00:01:04.364
We essentially were raising money

00:01:04.364 --> 00:01:05.865
for three weeks

00:01:05.865 --> 00:01:07.801
So we feel good about what we've done.

00:01:07.801 --> 00:01:09.135
There's also a super PAC

00:01:09.135 --> 00:01:12.872
that has been supporting our our effort,

00:01:13.473 --> 00:01:15.675
which raised another $6 million

00:01:16.142 --> 00:01:17.010
on top of that.

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:18.478
So I think we had a pretty good

00:01:18.478 --> 00:01:19.379
three weeks.

00:01:19.379 --> 00:01:20.780
I want to get your reaction to something

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:21.848
said by the Republican

00:01:21.848 --> 00:01:23.783
frontrunner, Donald Trump, last night

00:01:23.783 --> 00:01:25.051
about the criminal charges

00:01:25.051 --> 00:01:25.919
that he's facing now

00:01:25.919 --> 00:01:27.287
and perhaps charges

00:01:27.287 --> 00:01:28.922
that might be pending. Take a listen.

00:01:30.123 --> 00:01:31.357
Every time the radical

00:01:31.357 --> 00:01:32.425
left, Democrats,

00:01:32.425 --> 00:01:33.827
Marxists, communists

00:01:33.827 --> 00:01:35.929
and fascists, indict me,

00:01:35.929 --> 00:01:36.830
I consider it

00:01:36.830 --> 00:01:39.632
to be a great badge of honor and courage.

00:01:39.632 --> 00:01:42.302
I'm doing it for you.

00:01:42.302 --> 00:01:44.804
I'm being indicted for you.

00:01:44.804 --> 00:01:47.173
Better me than you, right?

00:01:47.173 --> 00:01:49.242
Great badge of honor and courage.

00:01:49.242 --> 00:01:50.743
Better than better me than you.

00:01:50.743 --> 00:01:52.479
What do you make of that?

00:01:54.681 --> 00:01:57.150
He's a liar and a coward.

00:01:57.150 --> 00:01:58.218
He's not giving interviews

00:01:58.218 --> 00:01:58.985
for anyone other

00:01:58.985 --> 00:02:01.287
than because of his own conduct.

00:02:01.287 --> 00:02:02.288
There's no other

00:02:02.288 --> 00:02:03.990
of the 200 million Americans

00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:05.191
you spoke about

00:02:05.191 --> 00:02:07.160
who illegally retained

00:02:07.160 --> 00:02:09.295
classified national secrets

00:02:09.596 --> 00:02:10.697
after being asked

00:02:10.697 --> 00:02:13.166
politely, quietly and professionally

00:02:13.466 --> 00:02:14.567
for 18 months

00:02:14.567 --> 00:02:15.401
to voluntarily

00:02:15.401 --> 00:02:16.636
turn them back over

00:02:16.636 --> 00:02:18.404
after he left the White House.

00:02:18.404 --> 00:02:19.472
There's no other of those

00:02:19.472 --> 00:02:20.907
200 million Americans

00:02:20.907 --> 00:02:22.575
who lied to their own lawyers

00:02:22.575 --> 00:02:24.544
about where those documents were.

00:02:24.544 --> 00:02:25.778
And there's none of those other

00:02:25.778 --> 00:02:27.347
200 million Americans

00:02:27.347 --> 00:02:29.482
who lied to the prosecutors about it

00:02:29.482 --> 00:02:31.551
and flashed around documents

00:02:31.551 --> 00:02:33.586
regarding an Iranian war plan

00:02:33.586 --> 00:02:34.487
to people who didn't have

00:02:34.487 --> 00:02:35.555
the clearance to see them.

00:02:36.556 --> 00:02:38.892
Look, he's indicted

00:02:38.892 --> 00:02:41.194
because of his outrageous conduct,

00:02:41.794 --> 00:02:43.463
and that's why he's been indicted.

00:02:43.463 --> 00:02:46.299
He now has the opportunity to go to court

00:02:46.900 --> 00:02:48.101
and make the government prove

00:02:48.101 --> 00:02:50.003
that case beyond a reasonable doubt.

00:02:50.003 --> 00:02:51.004
But now he says he doesn't

00:02:51.004 --> 00:02:51.771
want to have a trial

00:02:51.771 --> 00:02:54.541
until after the election in 20, 24.

00:02:55.008 --> 00:02:56.342
I don't think he's doing that for us

00:02:56.342 --> 00:02:56.943
either.

00:02:56.943 --> 00:02:58.144
He should resolve this thing

00:02:58.144 --> 00:02:59.512
before people vote

00:02:59.512 --> 00:03:00.713
so that we know exactly

00:03:00.713 --> 00:03:02.182
who we're voting for.

00:03:02.182 --> 00:03:03.283
To put behind the desk

00:03:03.283 --> 00:03:04.951
in the Oval Office.

00:03:04.951 --> 00:03:06.786
He says he's doing it for us.

00:03:06.786 --> 00:03:08.087
That's a lie.

00:03:08.087 --> 00:03:09.622
And what he was doing,

00:03:09.622 --> 00:03:10.890
all the things that he was doing

00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:11.991
with those documents

00:03:11.991 --> 00:03:13.826
it shows exactly what a coward he is.

00:03:13.826 --> 00:03:14.394
I know

00:03:14.394 --> 00:03:15.728
you just mentioned your super PAC

00:03:15.728 --> 00:03:16.596
and I know you're

00:03:16.596 --> 00:03:17.330
legally not allowed

00:03:17.330 --> 00:03:18.932
to coordinate with your super PAC.

00:03:18.932 --> 00:03:20.600
So you might be seeing this ad

00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:22.468
I'm about to play for the first time.

00:03:22.468 --> 00:03:23.770
But I want to play you a video

00:03:23.770 --> 00:03:24.737
that your super PAC is

00:03:24.737 --> 00:03:25.772
going to release tomorrow.

00:03:27.307 --> 00:03:29.275
Should you show up to the debate?

00:03:29.275 --> 00:03:30.543
Because if you do,

00:03:30.543 --> 00:03:31.277
your opponents

00:03:31.277 --> 00:03:32.979
will bring up the impeachment,

00:03:32.979 --> 00:03:34.514
the indictments,

00:03:34.514 --> 00:03:36.616
bring up how you lost to Joe Biden.

00:03:37.083 --> 00:03:39.452
So, Donald, you need to decide,

00:03:40.220 --> 00:03:43.856
are you a chicken or just a loser?

00:03:44.857 --> 00:03:46.993
They're calling him a chicken or a loser.

00:03:46.993 --> 00:03:47.927
I guess they have to

00:03:47.927 --> 00:03:49.495
he has to make a choice there.

00:03:49.495 --> 00:03:52.131
What's your reaction to this ad?

00:03:53.299 --> 00:03:54.133
Well, it's the first time

00:03:54.133 --> 00:03:54.634
I've seen it,

00:03:54.634 --> 00:03:55.435
but I think it's probably

00:03:55.435 --> 00:03:57.170
a pretty good question.

00:03:57.570 --> 00:03:59.672
And he should show up at the debates

00:03:59.672 --> 00:04:01.174
and defend his record.

00:04:01.174 --> 00:04:02.809
The Republican Party voters

00:04:02.809 --> 00:04:03.810
who are deciding

00:04:03.810 --> 00:04:06.012
who our nominee should be

00:04:06.012 --> 00:04:08.047
should be able to make that decision

00:04:08.047 --> 00:04:09.816
by comparing all the candidates

00:04:09.816 --> 00:04:12.285
who qualify for the debate stage

00:04:12.285 --> 00:04:13.653
right next to each other,

00:04:13.653 --> 00:04:15.521
challenging each other's records,

00:04:15.521 --> 00:04:16.856
discussing each other's plans

00:04:16.856 --> 00:04:18.391
for the future of America

00:04:18.391 --> 00:04:20.226
and how they're going to beat Joe Biden.

00:04:20.226 --> 00:04:21.461
And we're happy

00:04:21.461 --> 00:04:22.862
because now, Jake,

00:04:22.862 --> 00:04:25.465
almost 45,000 individual donors

00:04:25.698 --> 00:04:26.966
went to Chris Christie dot

00:04:26.966 --> 00:04:28.368
com and donated that.

00:04:28.368 --> 00:04:30.403
We have qualified for the debate stage

00:04:30.403 --> 00:04:32.305
will be there on August 23rd

00:04:32.305 --> 00:04:33.806
and we'll be waiting for Donald Trump.

00:04:33.806 --> 00:04:34.907
But let me be candid here.

00:04:34.907 --> 00:04:36.009
You are starting to gain

00:04:36.009 --> 00:04:37.644
some ground in New Hampshire.

00:04:37.644 --> 00:04:39.145
But Donald Trump is still leading by

00:04:39.145 --> 00:04:41.347
about 20 points just in New Hampshire.

00:04:41.581 --> 00:04:43.950
He's up in Iowa. He's up nationally.

00:04:44.250 --> 00:04:44.684
Is it

00:04:44.684 --> 00:04:45.718
not just a fact

00:04:45.718 --> 00:04:47.387
that as of now, Donald Trump remains

00:04:47.387 --> 00:04:48.021
far and away

00:04:48.021 --> 00:04:49.389
the choice of Republican voters?

00:04:49.389 --> 00:04:51.891
Even if you cannot understand why

00:04:54.961 --> 00:04:55.528
Well, no.

00:04:55.528 --> 00:04:56.429
The fact is that

00:04:56.429 --> 00:04:57.964
he's ahead in the polls right now, Jake.

00:04:57.964 --> 00:04:59.832
You have reported that accurately.

00:04:59.832 --> 00:05:01.034
I'll fact check you

00:05:01.034 --> 00:05:02.235
and that is a correct fact

00:05:02.235 --> 00:05:03.303
that you've put forward.

00:05:03.303 --> 00:05:04.237
But you know,

00:05:04.237 --> 00:05:05.204
the good news

00:05:05.204 --> 00:05:07.240
is that no one's voting in Iowa

00:05:07.240 --> 00:05:08.841
till January 15th.

00:05:08.841 --> 00:05:09.242
No one's

00:05:09.242 --> 00:05:10.476
probably early voting in New Hampshire

00:05:10.476 --> 00:05:12.712
till later that month or early February.

00:05:13.246 --> 00:05:15.415
And there's a lot of campaign to go here.

00:05:15.415 --> 00:05:15.815
In fact,

00:05:15.815 --> 00:05:17.116
we haven't even had the first debate

00:05:17.116 --> 00:05:18.318
yet, as you mentioned.

00:05:18.318 --> 00:05:19.052
So lots of August.

00:05:19.052 --> 00:05:20.019
23rd,

00:05:20.019 --> 00:05:21.587
I think most people, let's say in

00:05:21.587 --> 00:05:22.922
my region of the country

00:05:22.922 --> 00:05:25.325
are down to the Jersey Shore right now,

00:05:25.325 --> 00:05:26.993
enjoying their summer vacation,

00:05:26.993 --> 00:05:27.960
maybe in New Hampshire

00:05:27.960 --> 00:05:29.662
at Lake Winnipesaukee.

00:05:29.662 --> 00:05:30.963
They're not focused on this yet.

00:05:30.963 --> 00:05:31.364
Just you

00:05:31.364 --> 00:05:31.631
and I

00:05:31.631 --> 00:05:32.865
are in a few other

00:05:32.865 --> 00:05:35.168
candidates so let's get people focused

00:05:35.168 --> 00:05:36.069
when we get here.

00:05:36.069 --> 00:05:37.770
Late summer, early fall.

00:05:37.770 --> 00:05:39.072
Let's engage in intellectual.

00:05:39.072 --> 00:05:40.239
We talk about,

00:05:40.239 --> 00:05:42.775
you know, some very simple issues, Jake.

00:05:42.775 --> 00:05:44.610
You know, first is, you know,

00:05:44.610 --> 00:05:46.546
are you going to get the truth?

00:05:46.546 --> 00:05:47.580
You deserve the truth

00:05:47.580 --> 00:05:49.349
as a Republican primary voter

00:05:49.349 --> 00:05:50.983
and as an American.

00:05:50.983 --> 00:05:52.051
And will you get a candidate

00:05:52.051 --> 00:05:54.053
who will make the truth important?

00:05:54.053 --> 00:05:55.922
We know Donald Trump hasn't done that.

00:05:55.922 --> 00:05:56.422
And will you get

00:05:56.422 --> 00:05:58.057
someone who will deliver results

00:05:58.057 --> 00:06:00.159
on the issues that you care about?

00:06:00.159 --> 00:06:01.594
You know, Donald Trump was arguing again

00:06:01.594 --> 00:06:03.296
last night about immigration.

00:06:03.296 --> 00:06:03.996
He didn't do anything

00:06:03.996 --> 00:06:05.231
to change the immigration laws

00:06:05.231 --> 00:06:06.232
to make them better

00:06:06.232 --> 00:06:07.800
or stronger for America.

00:06:07.800 --> 00:06:10.636
And he built 47 miles of new wall.

00:06:10.870 --> 00:06:12.438
I mean, his four years as president

00:06:12.438 --> 00:06:13.206
you know, Jake,

00:06:13.206 --> 00:06:14.107
at that rate,

00:06:14.107 --> 00:06:16.642
he would need 110 more years as president

00:06:16.843 --> 00:06:18.378
to be able to finish the wall

00:06:18.378 --> 00:06:20.880
between the United States and Mexico.

00:06:20.880 --> 00:06:22.648
The first debate as you note, now

00:06:22.648 --> 00:06:23.449
almost a month away.

00:06:23.449 --> 00:06:24.484
I want you to take a listen to what

00:06:24.484 --> 00:06:24.984
your fellow

00:06:24.984 --> 00:06:27.019
2024 candidate, former Texas

00:06:27.019 --> 00:06:28.287
Congressman Will Hurd,

00:06:28.287 --> 00:06:28.921
had to say

00:06:28.921 --> 00:06:29.789
about those

00:06:29.789 --> 00:06:31.190
who take the debate pledge

00:06:31.190 --> 00:06:32.825
to support the eventual nominee.

00:06:32.825 --> 00:06:33.493
This is what he had to

00:06:33.493 --> 00:06:34.527
say a couple of weeks ago.

00:06:36.362 --> 00:06:37.530
I can't lie

00:06:37.530 --> 00:06:39.265
to get access to a microphone.

00:06:39.265 --> 00:06:41.467
I'm not going to support Donald Trump.

00:06:41.467 --> 00:06:42.869
I recognize the impact

00:06:42.869 --> 00:06:43.403
it has

00:06:43.403 --> 00:06:45.338
on on on my ability

00:06:45.338 --> 00:06:47.173
to get access to the debate stage.

00:06:47.173 --> 00:06:48.608
But I can't lie.

00:06:48.608 --> 00:06:50.443
It'll be easy to say I'll do it.

00:06:50.443 --> 00:06:51.844
And then when it comes down

00:06:51.844 --> 00:06:53.179
you know, change your mind.

00:06:53.179 --> 00:06:56.215
But I just can't I can't do that

00:06:56.215 --> 00:06:57.917
in your. I'm sorry.

00:06:57.917 --> 00:06:59.719
And Will Hurd's formulation,

00:06:59.719 --> 00:07:02.388
are you lying to make the debate stage

00:07:02.388 --> 00:07:03.222
by signing a pledge

00:07:03.222 --> 00:07:04.056
to support the nominee,

00:07:04.056 --> 00:07:05.258
no matter who it is, including

00:07:05.258 --> 00:07:06.692
if it's Donald Trump

00:07:08.494 --> 00:07:09.829
Well, I won't see,

00:07:09.829 --> 00:07:10.329
I won't see

00:07:10.329 --> 00:07:11.731
will hurt on the debate stage.

00:07:11.731 --> 00:07:13.366
And that's okay by me.

00:07:13.366 --> 00:07:14.634
The fact is, we've got to change

00:07:14.634 --> 00:07:16.936
our party, Jake, and change our country.

00:07:17.537 --> 00:07:19.405
And we had these debate pledges

00:07:20.373 --> 00:07:20.907
eight years

00:07:20.907 --> 00:07:22.542
ago, as you'll recall,

00:07:22.542 --> 00:07:24.243
and all of us sign them.

00:07:24.243 --> 00:07:26.646
And then when we got on the debate stage

00:07:26.646 --> 00:07:27.880
and we were asked to reaffirm

00:07:27.880 --> 00:07:28.981
it, Donald Trump

00:07:28.981 --> 00:07:30.416
refused to raise his hand.

00:07:30.416 --> 00:07:31.818
The only one of the ten candidates

00:07:31.818 --> 00:07:32.652
who did.

00:07:32.852 --> 00:07:34.020
The fact is,

00:07:34.020 --> 00:07:35.688
he has set the precedent here.

00:07:35.688 --> 00:07:37.757
And I will sign the debate pledge

00:07:38.291 --> 00:07:39.325
and I will take it every bit

00:07:39.325 --> 00:07:41.694
as seriously as he did in 2016.

00:07:42.261 --> 00:07:43.429
New Jersey Governor Chris Christie,

00:07:43.429 --> 00:07:44.530
thanks so much for joining us today.

00:07:44.530 --> 00:07:45.631
Appreciate it.

00:07:47.366 --> 00:07:48.401
Jake, thanks for having me.

00:07:48.401 --> 00:07:49.035
I appreciate it.

